4.1 The confidentiality obligations in Clause 2 do not apply to any Information that the Recipient can verify by written evidence:
4.1.1 is already publicly known at the time of disclosure, or subsequently enters the public domain without fault or breach by the Recipient or its Representatives;
4.1.2 was already lawfully known to the Recipient prior to disclosure by the Discloser, without restriction on use or disclosure;
4.1.3 is received in good faith from an independent third party who is entitled to make such disclosure without breaching any legal or fiduciary duty; or
4.1.4 was independently developed by the Recipient's employees or contractors who had no access to or knowledge of the Discloser's Confidential Information.
